Four hundred sites is not four hundred problems — it is one problem, four hundred times. The
migration paid off once the shared shell existed; everything after that was mechanical.

![Placeholder](../../src/assets/placeholder-2.jpg)

SEO and analytics parity were non-negotiable, so every migrated site shipped with a redirect
map and a before/after Lighthouse run.

![Placeholder](../../src/assets/placeholder-2.jpg)
